@startuml
title PayLink - Refund a completed payment (FR-27, payment stays COMPLETED)
' Names follow docs/design/glossary.md, architecture.md (section 4.2) and class-diagram.puml.
' Decisions: D-12 (separate RefundRequest process, payment status does not change),
' D-13 (the fee is returned, refund = totalAmount), D-14 (agent commission is reversed,
' PayLink absorbs the difference), D-18 (refund is paid from the SYSTEM wallet), D-17 (AuditLog is append-only).
' No payment state changes here, so none of the 9 transitions of brief 2.5 is used and no PaymentStatusHistory is written.
' D-13, D-14 and D-18 are marked "team to confirm" in requirements.md.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor "Customer" as Cust
actor "SupportUser" as Sup
participant "PaymentService" as PS
participant "WalletService" as Wal

== 1. The customer asks for a refund (US-27.1, US-27.4) ==
Cust -> PS : requestRefund(paymentId, customerId, reason)
PS -> PS : find(paymentId)
alt the payment is not COMPLETED, or it is not the customer's payment
  PS --> Cust : refused, no RefundRequest is created
  note right of PS
    FAILED payments are refunded by the normal flow
    (see the refund-a-failed-payment diagram).
    UNKNOWN is never refunded.
  end note
else the payment already has an APPROVED RefundRequest
  PS --> Cust : refused (a payment is paid back only once)
else the payment is COMPLETED
  PS -> PS : create RefundRequest status PENDING (reason, createdAt)
  PS --> Cust : request received
  note right of PS
    The payment stays COMPLETED (final state).
    No money moves yet.
  end note
end

== 2a. Support rejects the request (US-27.3) ==
Sup -> PS : rejectRefund(requestId, supportId, reason)
alt the RefundRequest is not PENDING
  PS --> Sup : refused (already decided)
else the RefundRequest is PENDING
  PS -> PS : RefundRequest status REJECTED\n(decisionReason, decidedAt)
  PS -> PS : AuditLog entry (who, when, why)
  note right of PS
    No money moves.
  end note
end

== 2b. Support approves the request (US-27.2) ==
Sup -> PS : approveRefund(requestId, supportId, reason)
alt the RefundRequest is not PENDING
  PS --> Sup : refused (approving twice never pays twice)
else the RefundRequest is PENDING
  PS -> Wal : reverseCompleted(paymentId, requestId, supportId)
  note over Wal
    One database transaction.
    Reads the LedgerEntries of the payment
    (DEBIT, FEE_INCOME and, if an agent was involved, COMMISSION)
    and posts one REVERSAL entry for each. Nothing is edited or deleted.
  end note
  Wal -> Wal : REVERSAL on the customer wallet\n(availableDelta = +totalAmount, fee included)
  Wal -> Wal : REVERSAL on the SYSTEM wallet\n(returns the fee income and pays the amount the biller already kept)
  opt the payment had an agent Commission
    Wal -> Wal : REVERSAL on the agent wallet\n(only what the agent still has available)
    note right of Wal
      If the agent already spent part of it, PayLink absorbs
      the difference (D-14). The agent wallet never goes negative.
    end note
  end
  Wal -> Wal : AuditLog entry for every REVERSAL\n(who, when, why, refId = LedgerEntry id)
  Wal --> PS : done
  PS -> PS : RefundRequest status APPROVED\n(decisionReason, decidedAt)
  PS -> PS : AuditLog entry (who, when, why)
  note right of PS
    COMPLETED is final and REFUNDED comes only from FAILED,
    so the payment status does not change.
  end note
end
@enduml
